g but he had that overturned too  speaking with the new york times this  year he framed himself as a bringer of  stability but said little on policy safe  had been imprisoned for war crimes and  just this month the international  criminal court reminded the world that  he is wanted for alleged crimes against  humanity and he is certainly  an ideological lightning rod in libya he  he really does cut right down the  dividing line between those that want to  transition towards a democratic and an  equitable libya um and those that just  want to see it run by  you know certain tribes and certain  members of the of libya's communities  that may  ride in first class in an authoritarian  boat whilst leading everyone else in  coach there are dozens of candidates  including others who've spent time in  canada analysts say as long as foreign  powers continue to have a military  influence in libya the country will  remain divided and ultimately lawless  what's very important that we have to  take back this legitimacy that we have  given to these militias to these  criminals libya's outgoing united  nations mediator thinks the country  needs a vote as soon as possible as the  u.n security council remains divided on  its strategy for this troubled north  african nation redmond shannon global  news london  does plexiglas provide proper protection  from kovid and how can you safely  socialize with unvaccinated friends and  family over the holidays the experts  answer your covid questions after the  break  [Music]  we've heard growing calls from health  officials in recent days for people to  upgrade their masks to protect against  omicron but what exactly makes the mask  the right fit to answer that question  and others we've received from our  viewers over the past few days we are  joined now by infectious diseases  physician dr isaac bogash and  epidemiologist patrick saunders hastings  doctors thank you both so much for  joining us to tackle some of these  questions so isaac bogash first over to  you for those of us who put masks on our  christmas list this year fred wants to  know is mass quality more important with  omicron and what's acceptable and when  should a mask be discarded or washed  what do you think  yeah a couple of points here a higher  quality mask certainly is uh is more  important especially with omicron where  we have very little wiggle room uh as  this is a very transmissible variant uh  higher quality means something better  than a single layered cloth mask you  might hear words like n95 or kn95  it's thicker they've got less pores in  them and the key thing here is it's got  a tighter fit around around the nose and  around the mouth and that's really it a  good a tight fit around the face and a  higher caliber mask and 95 kn 95  sometimes you hear surgical masks as  well and again  these uh n95s and kn95s have usually a  much tighter fit than the surgical mask  too  yeah very good to know dr saunders  hastings over to you for the next  related question this one comes from  lisa who says that she works in an  office with several people sitting next  to each other not wearing masks but  there are plexiglass barriers in between  them does plexiglas help protect against  omicron it does help protect i think  like masks plexiglass can be a tool in a  tool set of preventing transmission but  i think like masks they are not  foolproof and then they are not 100  effective and so i think  we're often better served considering  plexiglas is part of a broader suite of  transmission prevention protocols  including masks and so i think when  we're talking about office settings  depending on the crowded nature the  ventilation  other protocols in place  plexiglas may or may not be sufficient  but it certainly doesn't hurt and it can  help to prevent transmission  okay uh dr bergash back over to you for  this next question that comes from judy  an interesting one she says if someone  has kovid but doesn't know it perhaps  they're a